<article class="collection"><nav><a href="/en/">English edition</a> / Themes</nav><p class="kicker">LITERATURE · HISTORY · READING PATHS</p><h1>Six ways to read Martín Fierro</h1><p class="lead">These six editorial themes help readers follow questions across the poem without treating them as original divisions by José Hernández. Each connects critical commentary, a question and an authentic Spanish passage.</p><div class="cards">{englishThemes.map((x,i)=><section><p class="kicker">READING PATH {i+1}</p><h2><a href={`/en/themes/${x.slug}/`}>{x.title}</a></h2><p>{x.lead}</p><a href={`/en/themes/${x.slug}/`}>Explore this theme →</a></section>)}</div><p>For the wider critical context, consult <a href="/en/exegesis/">English exegesis</a> and the <a href="/en/students/">46 canto guides</a>.</p></article>
